 "base": "art/",
 "note": "Pictures under the reading (art.js). A scene starts on the cue whose n equals 'from' and lasts until the next; an empty images list ends the pictures. Chapter II pilot, 17 Oct 2026: Midjourney stills by Ian, style-referenced to the Demeter voyage. Chapter I (17 Oct): the warm daylight journey, style-referenced to voyage/varna-1.jpg; the night at the pass style-referenced to storm-1.jpg. The four 'red lips' close-ups came out as a woman's face and are left out. Chapter III (20 Oct): 63 Midjourney stills by Ian, style-referenced to the voyage harbour paintings; the hand-washing warning (cues 31–34) left without its own picture by Ian's choice — the letters hold until the Count goes out of the window. Chapter IV (20 Oct): 78 stills by Ian. Midjourney gave the Count a white beard in Part I; Ian accepted it for the castle chapters — he is groomed and younger for London in Part II. Cues 50–59 (the Count announcing the parting) reuse two of the three-letters paintings; cues 71–74 reuse the wall climb. Lamp, fire, mist and water loops (20 Oct): 15 twelve-second loops made by Claude from the lead paintings (dracula/*-air.mp4 on the Media Door) — the flame moves only where the flame is. Ch 1–2 loops and the moon skies (20 Oct, evening): 13 more loops for chapters 1–2; the three clear-sky moon scenes (ch03 f1-3, f2-2; ch04 g1-3) re-made as -air2 with thin clouds drifting across the moon, twinkling stars and one steady bright planet. Sky effects are only where the sky is open — never across branches or walls.",
